                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "234472770",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561199218109155",
                            "num_reviews": 197,
                            "playtime_forever": 219,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 219,
                            "last_played": 1788548549
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The main character is a weird little pumpkin-looking guy, and I really liked the unusual art style and character designs. The whole game has a strange and mysterious atmosphere. The gameplay is pretty straightforward: you explore different areas, interact with objects and characters, collect items, and look around the environment for clues. Some puzzles can be solved by examining your surroundings and putting the clues together. However, I found the puzzles much harder than those in most puzzle games I’ve played. The game doesn’t always give you enough information to point you in the right direction, so some solutions can feel pretty random or difficult to figure out on your own. A few puzzles suddenly become much more challenging and may take quite a few tries. The game also has multiple endings, which is a nice touch if you want to see everything. One thing I’d recommend is saving at Chapters 6 and 7, so you can go back and try the different endings without having to replay a big part of the game.",
